    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "202128aa_2a242322",
        "filename": "board/fizz/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-03T22:53:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What do you think about limiting the source current to 1.5A in S0 and to 3.0A in S3/S5? We will change charge_manager_source_port so that it will call board_vbus_update_source_current with different Rp based on the power state.",
      "parentUuid": "d1100fb1_48cfaa31",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "debe9b6264450307a976d330edcc6483ac74dc14",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88252a76_1c03c850",
        "filename": "board/fizz/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000016
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-03T22:55:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t know the power/thermal budget on this product.\nWe cannot do 3.0A all the time ?",
      "parentUuid": "202128aa_2a242322",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "debe9b6264450307a976d330edcc6483ac74dc14",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ad43f10e_a2fa5a18",
        "filename": "board/fizz/usb_pd_policy.c",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 59,
      "author": {
        "id": 1106949
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-04T00:32:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We\u0027re a bit careful about power budget because Fizz doesn\u0027t have a battery. So, we need a head room to dodge spikes. I think our choice would be either all 1.5A or 1.5A/3.0A but not all 3.0A.\n\nWe prefer providing 3.0A. So, the circuit will be there. We don\u0027t have to make the decision now. If the OS is smart enough to manage power, it\u0027ll be able to send command to the ec to switch between 1.5/3.0A. If not, we\u0027ll make it 1.5A all the time.",
      "parentUuid": "88252a76_1c03c850",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 59,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 59,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "debe9b6264450307a976d330edcc6483ac74dc14",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
